# ===========================================================================
# What belongs in the repository
# ===========================================================================
#   tracked   source, docs, and the *_example.txt templates
#   ignored   anything a command regenerates, anything personal, any test file
#
# The rule of thumb: if running a command recreates it, it does not belong in
# git. Every ignored file here is reproduced by a documented command.
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests â€” never committed. Verification comes from running the real pipeline
# with different arguments (see commands.md, "Recipes"), not from a suite that
# can drift away from the code it claims to cover.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/
test/
*_test.py
test_*.py
*_tests.py
tests.py
conftest.py
pytest.ini
tox.ini
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal config â€” real files ignored, templates tracked.
#
# Copy the template, fill it in:
#   copy player_example.txt player.txt
#   copy process_api\api_example.txt process_api\api.txt
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
player.txt
api.txt
api_*.txt
api-*.txt
!api_example.txt
!process_api/api_example.txt

# Belt and braces for the same idea, in case a credential file turns up later.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials*.json
secrets*.json
secrets*.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# process_api/ â€” the source is tracked, everything it writes is not.
#
# The incremental fetcher's scripts are part of the project, so they belong in
# git. Its data/ directory does not: `python -m process_api.cli` recreates every
# byte of it, and it names the account and every game uuid.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
process_api/data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Engines and models â€” ~1 GB of third-party binaries, all re-downloadable.
#   python setup.py  puts every one of these back and verifies the install.
#   StockFish : github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish -> engines\stockfish\
#   Lc0       : github.com/LeelaChessZero/lc0           -> engines\lc0-gpu\
#   Lc0 nets  : lczero.org/play/networks/bestnets/       -> data\nets\
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
engines/
data/

# Belt and braces, in case an engine or net is dropped somewhere else.
stockfish.exe
stockfish
lc0.exe
lc0
*.nnue
*.nnue.embedded
*.pb
*.pb.gz
*.onnx
DirectML.dll

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.installed.cfg
pip-wheel-metadata/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pipeline output â€” every file here is written by analyze.py / report.py
#   python analyze.py --player me --out out
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
out/
out_*/
report.html
data.json
annotated.pgn
raw.pgn

# Personal game archive from fetch_games.py. games/opera.pgn (the Morphy
# reference game the README verification steps use) is tracked on purpose.
games/raw*.pgn

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent / editor / tool config â€” machine-local, not part of the project
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.opencode/
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
.specstory/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md
mcp.json
.mcp.json
opencode.json

.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Caches, logs, OS cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.cache/
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
nohup.out
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Ignore Plans folder (.md files with specs to AI)
plans/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node -- the React frontend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# node_modules/ is reproducible from ui/package.json, and ui/dist/ is written by
# `npm run build`. Both are recreated by any of:
#   python report.py --standalone      npm install + npm run build
#   python serve.py --build            the same, without the data
#   python serve.py --dev              Vite's dev server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/

